2. Official requirements rechecked (accessed 2026-09-22)

- AIP Author Instructions:
  https://publishing.aip.org/resources/researchers/author-instructions/
  Mandatory manuscript order is title/authors/affiliations, abstract, text,
  conclusion, acknowledgments, author declarations, data availability,
  appendixes, references. COI and CRediT statements are mandatory. Tables must
  be captioned, cited, and numbered consecutively with Roman numerals.
  Single-appendix equations use (A1), (A2), etc.; appendix figures/tables
  continue main-text numbering. JMP authors “should use” the JMP Overleaf
  template, while the initial submission format is one compiled PDF; template
  conversion was not undertaken in this focused task.
- Research Data Policy:
  https://publishing.aip.org/resources/researchers/open-science/research-data-policy/
  A Data Availability statement is mandatory, but it must accurately identify
  public material or use another applicable AIP template. A remote URL alone is
  not evidence that the repository is publicly accessible and sufficient.
- Accessibility guidance:
  https://publishing.aip.org/resources/researchers/policies-and-ethics/accessibility/
  Alt text is required for publication. The implementation instruction says
  that upon revision authors submit a separate `.txt` or `.docx` mapping for
  every required visual element. Therefore no undocumented LaTeX macro was
  invented; `manuscript/jmp_alt_text.txt` was created for author verification.
- JMP-specific graphics guidance on the Author Instructions page sets a
  one-column maximum width of 6.69 inches and minimum label size guidance.
  Existing figures fit the current one-column layout; no figure was altered.

